{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact CUT-R R1 preparation head 4dabb18c7b097f4a2bdac0bc82ab8a80ef2e6d78 on builder/cut-r-r1-20261114, all 30 artifacts, for request fef6bd59 under implementation promise 6646de25 and my promise dd6332b4. R1 keeps the earlier signed Grow packet as an immutable fixture, separates the earlier constants from the current ones, and pins the source identifiers of Grow, Lending and Counter. Today it changes no running behavior. It creates no release, signs nothing and deploys nothing.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The production changes. `apps/room/worker.grow.ts` and `examples/grow/simulator-worker.ts` rename the imported packet binding to `currentPacket` and change nothing else. `examples/grow/simulator-host.ts` binds the historical-pin exception to `EARLIER_GROW_RELEASE` and `EARLIER_GROW_PUBLISHER` instead of `DEMO_RELEASE` and `DEMO_PUBLISHER`. Both pairs hold the same values today, and the site and room pins keep the same digests in the same order. A current or TEST release still compares against the maintained source. `scripts/format-json.mjs` adds the fixture to `CANONICAL_PROTOCOL_PACKETS`, so the formatter never rewrites its signed bytes.\n- The fixture. `examples/grow/fixtures/earlier-application.dap.json` has blob b2c7cf62. That blob equals `examples/grow/demo/application.dap.json` at this head and at main 11c215a4, byte for byte.\n- The seals. `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` changes exactly the three seals that root act 707b3ca3 adopts: `worker.grow.ts`, `simulator-worker.ts` and `simulator-host.ts`. I reviewed the three source diffs behind them, as set out above. They add no provider, credential, configuration or trust.\n- The reproduction witness. `application-release-reproduction.test.ts` prepares each application through `prepareApplicationDirectory` with a public TEST signer, then compares entry, sorted definitions, semantic and presentation identifiers with the committed `release-identifiers.json`. It compares no signature or release digest, as the note says.\n- Historical witnesses. The archive, codec, corpus and simulator tests now name the fixture and the earlier constants. `recorded-grow-release.ts` becomes `earlier-grow-release.ts` with the same release, publisher and entry.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 11c215a4 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The head changes 30 paths. Each path has an artifact at the head, including the deleted `recorded-grow-release.ts`.\n- Integration. Merge 91f9cfbc has parents 0fed5793 and 11c215a4. `git merge-tree` of the two gives 61e9a17c, which equals the merge tree. From 91f9cfbc to the head, only the note and two manifests change, so the documentation-only follow-up rule applies.\n- Evidence. The five manifests list 175 files: focused 73, formatter preflight 3, formatter follow-up 25, gate 63, documentation checks 11. Every file matches its SHA-256 and byte count, and `SHA256SUMS` verifies in all five directories. The gate and documentation manifests hash to 66e1b047 and 95162d7d, as the request states. The gate at 91f9cfbc wrote exit 0 and ends \"gate passed\", with no timeout line. All 77 in-run samples and both endpoints read AC Power, and every reading shows powermode 0. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 04:00 to 06:00 EST. The maintained selector included the scale cases (`changed-scale-path`, three matched paths) without force. `closure-coverage.json` shows a passed module for each native closure file.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 11 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One immutable fixture and one set of earlier constants now stand for the deployed signed packet. Each historical witness names them, so a later current release can change without rewriting history. The reproduction witness runs the one pack path, so a later head that changes a packed closure must refresh its identifiers in the same head, as ruling 119140cd requires.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The three seal changes cover renames and one constant binding with unchanged values. One fact for R2: `worker.grow.ts` builds its archive policies from `currentPacket` with `TRUSTED` = `DEMO_RELEASE`, `DEMO_PUBLISHER` and `GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS[0]`, and `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` names the earlier release. When R2 changes the current packet and `DEMO_RELEASE`, the archive's trusted release and its policy packet must still be the earlier signed install, or old archives lose their proof. The note states that old archives need the earlier proof. R2 must show where the Worker reads it.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Until R2, `DEMO_RELEASE` equals `EARLIER_GROW_RELEASE`, and `GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS` equals `EARLIER_GROW_DEFINITIONS`. The duplication is deliberate, because R2 changes only the current set. R2 could make `GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS` import the earlier constants, so that one name holds each digest.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing, signing, public-packet completion or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:29343c596355d4bc08e3ab1cdf450c6e99be9cd2","binding":"assigned","head":"4dabb18c7b097f4a2bdac0bc82ab8a80ef2e6d78","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd6332b48b5df1a9494913a1ed8e91ad1e543d45\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6646de25b81add51be70eafdad7c954ec1a01c4d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dfdb6b3484363cdb1121e8807c325e54a837195e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:118136ee4447898003c7af1b6033e45df0ceb1db, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ccc9012747837a2f95411d367c439e219d167a9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1cdc150d57b1944018ec6